Spec: CourseRealization entity and weekly view

Purpose:
  The CourseRealization entity: one offering of a Course, taught during one Semester for one group. It is the hub
  that ties a Course and a Semester to the Lessons taught in it. For example, the Course `Machine Learning` has a
  realization for group `TTV24SP` during the fall 2026 Semester; that realization is what the Lessons actually taught
  in that offering reference. The package also owns the per-CourseRealization weekly table (one row per calendar
  week, with `Week`, `Lessons` and `Deadline` columns), the single view a visitor or the admin lands on
  to see one
  realization's Lessons, resolving ../courses/courses.sdd's former open decision in favor of "one selected
  realization" over an aggregated per-Course or date-range view. Creating, editing and removing one is driven from
  ../courses/courses.sdd's page, which lists a Course's realizations.

Owns:
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py
  ./view.py
  ./routes.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  ../auth/auth.sdd
  ../courses/courses.sdd
  ../semester/semester.sdd
  ../lessons/lessons.sdd
  ../holidays/holidays.sdd
  ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd
  ../week_themes/week_themes.sdd
  ../deadlines/deadlines.sdd
  ../conferences/conferences.sdd
  ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd

Must:
  A CourseRealization has a reference to exactly one Course, a reference to exactly one Semester and a free-text
  group label such as `TTV24SP`. Both references are stored as plain ids in ./domain.py, per ../architecture.sdd;
  only ./services.py imports ../courses/courses.sdd's and ../semester/semester.sdd's ports.py to validate them.
  Both references are declared as foreign keys on the table, so the database enforces them and cascades a deleted
  Course or Semester to its realizations. The group label lives in the `group_label` column because `group` is a
  reserved SQL keyword; ./domain.py's @CourseRealization keeps the `group` attribute and ./repository_sqlite.py
  maps between the two.
  @CourseRealizationRepository in ./ports.py exposes operations to list realizations for a Course or a Semester and to
    add, update and remove one.
  A Course's realizations are listed across every Semester through @RealizationService, which labels each one from
  its group and its Semester, so ../courses/courses.sdd's page never reads this package's repository or domain
  directly.
  A CourseRealization's display label is composed from its Course name, group and Semester at render time; it is not
  stored as its own field.
  @RealizationService.add_realization validates that the Course and Semester ids exist and that the group label is
    non-empty, rejecting with @UnknownCourseError, @UnknownSemesterError or @InvalidRealizationError before storage.
  @RealizationService.update_realization re-labels an existing realization from a new group and Semester, validates
    them the same way and keeps the realization's Course, because ../courses/courses.sdd's edit dialog edits a
    realization from inside its own Course.
  @RealizationService.delete_realization removes a realization, rejecting an unknown id with
    @UnknownRealizationError; the database's `course_realization_id` foreign keys take its
    ../lessons/lessons.sdd Lessons and its ../deadlines/deadlines.sdd Deadlines with it, so nothing is left pointing
    at it.
  Each Lesson references exactly one CourseRealization; a CourseRealization's Lessons are found by querying
    ../lessons/lessons.sdd's service for that CourseRealization, not through a stored list.
  The table is created automatically on startup when it does not exist.
  ./routes.py registers the weekly view at `/realizations`, reading the Semester to filter by from the
  `semester_id` query parameter and the realization to show from the `realization_id` query parameter, so a link to
  one realization's weekly view is shareable; when `semester_id` is absent or unknown, the active Semester is the
  known `realization_id`'s own Semester when one is given, otherwise ../semester/semester.sdd's default-selection
  rule; when `realization_id` is absent, unknown, or belongs to another Semester, the view falls back to the first
  realization of the active Semester.
  ./routes.py passes the Semester options and the active Semester's id to ../shared/shared.sdd's persistent
  Semester selector, so switching the Semester filters the realizations shown; the weekly view's realization
  dropdown lists only the realizations of the active Semester, never every realization ever created, to avoid
  clutter; switching either dropdown updates its own query parameter without a full page reload and preserves the
  other.
  Each week is one table row: a `Week` column with the ISO week number (in a larger, dominant font) and the week's
  date range underneath, a `Lessons` column and a rightmost `Deadline` column; there is no separate `Notes` column. A
  week with more than one Lesson (or a Lesson and a Holiday) shows one sub-row per entry under that single week; the
  `Week` cell spans all of that week's sub-rows (`rowspan`) so it still reads as one row. A Lesson sub-row shows its
  topic, under it one line reading the Lesson's abbreviated weekday, its `d.m.` day and its time range, such as
  `Mon 21.9. 08:00\u201310:00`, and, under that line, its free-text note when it has one; the day omits the year
  because the row's `Week` cell already carries the week's full date range. A Holiday, read through
  ../holidays/holidays.sdd, shows its title in the `Lessons` column over a second line carrying that Holiday's own
  abbreviated weekday and `d.m.` day, such as `Wed 21.10.`, in red italics instead of the black of a Lesson, with no
  time range or note. A ../conferences/conferences.sdd Conference, read through that package, is laid out the same way
  as a Holiday and in the same place, only in purple instead of red, since it blocks no teaching; a day carrying both
  shows one sub-row for each. A visitor's week with neither shows a single empty sub-row.
  A week's `Week` cell shows that week's ../week_themes/week_themes.sdd WeekTheme, when one exists, on the same line
  as the week number, with the date range on the line below; the theme is shown to visitors and the admin alike, and
  a week without one shows no placeholder.
  The week row containing today carries a green bar along its left edge; no other week row does.
  A NoTeachWeek of the realization's Semester, read through ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd, consumes its whole
  week: that week shows exactly one sub-row whose `Lessons` cell reads the NoTeachWeek's title; no Lesson sub-row is
  shown for it, because no Lesson is ever added inside a NoTeachWeek.
  Every sub-row of such a week carries the mild red background tint that ../semester/semester.sdd's wall planner gives
    a blocked day row, so the week reads as blocked without reading its title; the tint is shown to visitors and the
    admin alike and no other week row carries it. Hovering a tinted admin week row deepens the red instead of turning
    gray, so the week stays visibly blocked while the pointer is on it.
  Clicking a lesson square in ../semester/semester.sdd's wall planner navigates to this view with that lesson's
    `realization_id`.
  ./view.py and ./routes.py depend on ../lessons/lessons.sdd even though ../lessons/lessons.sdd also depends on this
    package: this is the same safe join-entity pattern as the ../courses/courses.sdd and ../semester/semester.sdd
    mutual dependencies, since ./domain.py and ./ports.py never import another feature and only ./services.py crosses
    the boundary.
  For the admin, clicking a Lesson sub-row opens that Lesson's edit dialog; clicking the empty add slot at the bottom
    of a week's `Lessons` column opens ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd's add-Lesson form for that week, defaulting to the
    week's Monday and to the shown realization, with ../shared/shared.sdd's @day_calendar to pick the actual day; a
    week blocked by a NoTeachWeek and every visitor's week carry no add slot, and a visitor is shown neither trigger.
  Clicking a week row's `Week` cell is the admin's affordance for that week's ../week_themes/week_themes.sdd
    WeekTheme: it opens that week's own `<dialog>`, which offers the add form when the week has no theme and the edit
    form prefilled with the stored title when it has one. A visitor's `Week` cell carries no such trigger.
  The `Week` cell's dialog posts to `/realizations/week-themes` for a new theme and to
    `/realizations/week-themes/{week_theme_id}` for an edited one, and its `Delete` control confirms before posting
    to `/realizations/week-themes/{week_theme_id}/delete`, naming the theme and its week. These routes write through
    ../week_themes/week_themes.sdd's @WeekThemeService and, like the per-Lesson routes, redirect back to the shown
    realization's weekly view carrying a rejected write's message as an `error` query parameter. Those dialogs sit
    beside the weekly table rows inside its swap target, like the per-Lesson dialogs; a write, which swaps only the
    bare table, leaves every control and its dialog in place, and a write is rejected by ../auth/auth.sdd's guard for
    a non-admin session and leaves the WeekTheme unstored.
  A successful write re-renders the weekly table in place: the table carries the id
    ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd's @WEEK_TABLE_ID names as the dialog's swap target in this view.
  A Lesson sub-row is the admin's edit trigger: clicking it opens that Lesson's `<dialog>`, whose date field is
    ../shared/shared.sdd's @day_calendar, a Monday-first month grid with that Lesson's date checked, whose start time
    and end time are prefilled ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd's @time_select dropdowns side by side on one row, and whose
    topic and notes fields are prefilled, posting to `/realizations/lessons/{lesson_id}`, which writes through
    ../lessons/lessons.sdd's @LessonService.update_lesson and keeps the Lesson in the CourseRealization it already
    belongs to. A Holiday, Conference or NoTeachWeek sub-row is not clickable, since ../lessons/lessons.sdd owns only
    Lesson writes.
  The edit dialog carries a `Delete` control that closes the edit dialog and opens a confirmation `<dialog>` naming
    the Lesson's topic and date, posting to `/realizations/lessons/{lesson_id}/delete`, which writes through
    @LessonService.delete_lesson and leaves the realization and its other Lessons in place.
  The per-Lesson dialogs sit inside the weekly table's swap target, so a dialog write, which swaps only the bare
    table, leaves the week cells' own controls and the add slot in place.
  Both routes redirect back to the shown realization's weekly view, carrying the validation message from
    ../lessons/lessons.sdd as an `error` query parameter that this view renders above the table; a write is rejected
    by ../auth/auth.sdd's guard for a non-admin session and leaves the Lesson unstored.
  ./routes.py must not crash when ../semester/semester.sdd has no active Semester at all (none created yet); it
    renders ./view.py's `no_semester_state()` immediately in that case instead of dereferencing a Semester, while an
    active Semester without CourseRealizations renders `empty_state()`.
  The weekly view shows one Share button for every visitor and for the admin, above the weekly table; clicking it
    copies the canonical absolute URL of the shown realization, built by ./routes.py from the request's base URL and
    the resolved selection, so the copied link always carries both `realization_id` and `semester_id` even when the
    current address bar carries only one of them.
  The weekly view also shows a `Hide Conferences`/`Show Conferences` toggle and a `Hide Holidays`/`Show Holidays`
    toggle left of the Share button, for visitors and the admin alike. A visitor's weekly view starts with Conferences
    and Holidays hidden and the admin's starts with them shown; each toggle switches its own kind and relabels itself.
    Only a Conference and a single-day Holiday are affected: a NoTeachWeek, a Lesson and a Deadline stay visible
    whichever way the toggles are set.
  The toggles and the hidden state sit outside ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd's @WEEK_TABLE_ID, so a dialog write,
    which swaps only the weekly table, leaves them in place. A hidden kind is hidden through the content inside its
    `Lessons` cell, never by removing the cell from the table grid, so a hidden entry never shifts a later sub-row's
    Lesson into the `Deadline` column; the cell drops its padding instead, so its row collapses to the row border.
  The Share button's URL and label sit outside ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd's @WEEK_TABLE_ID, so a dialog write,
    which swaps only the weekly table, leaves the button in place.
  The rightmost column is `Deadline` and carries the realization's ../deadlines/deadlines.sdd Deadlines: a Deadline
    shows in the `Deadline` cell of the row of the week it falls in, with its title over its `d.m.yyyy` date, and a
    week with none leaves the cell blank. The cell spans that week's sub-rows (`rowspan`) like the `Week` cell, and
    both are shown to visitors and the admin alike.
  For the admin, the `Deadline` cell is also the trigger adding a Deadline to that week: it opens that week row's own
    `<dialog>`, whose date field is ../shared/shared.sdd's @day_calendar over that week's Monday and whose title
    field is empty. Each listed Deadline carries its own `Edit` and `Delete` controls, which stop the click's
    propagation first so they do not open that week's add dialog behind their own.
  `Edit` opens a `<dialog>` whose date field is @day_calendar with that Deadline's date checked and whose title is
    prefilled, posting to `/realizations/deadlines/{deadline_id}`, which writes through
    ../deadlines/deadlines.sdd's @DeadlineService.update_deadline and keeps the Deadline in the realization it
    already belongs to. `Delete` opens a confirmation `<dialog>` naming the Deadline and its date, posting to
    `/realizations/deadlines/{deadline_id}/delete`, which writes through @DeadlineService.delete_deadline and
    leaves the realization and its other entries in place.
  A week row's add dialog posts to `/realizations/deadlines`, which writes through @DeadlineService.add_deadline.
    Like the per-Lesson and per-week theme routes, all three routes redirect back to the shown realization's weekly
    view carrying a rejected write's message as an `error` query parameter, a write is rejected by
    ../auth/auth.sdd's guard for a non-admin session and leaves the Deadline unstored, and every one of these
    dialogs sits inside the weekly table's swap target, so a write leaves the cell's trigger and its dialogs in
    place.

Scenario: Deleting a realization takes its Lessons with it
  Given a CourseRealization has two Lessons
  When @RealizationService.delete_realization removes it
  Then neither Lesson remains for that CourseRealization

Scenario: Admin deletes one Lesson from the weekly view
  Given a CourseRealization's weekly table shows two Lessons
  And the admin is logged in
  When the admin clicks the first Lesson and confirms the delete dialog its edit dialog opened, which names the
    Lesson and its date
  Then the weekly table shows the other Lesson and the realization keeps both its Course and its other entries

Scenario: Admin adds a Lesson from a week's empty add slot
  Given a CourseRealization's weekly table shows a week without a Lesson
  And the admin is logged in
  When the admin clicks the week's empty add slot, picks the day on the Monday-first calendar, enters a topic, a start
    time and an end time and submits
  Then the weekly table re-renders in place with the new Lesson in that week

Scenario: Admin themes one week from the weekly view
  Given a CourseRealization's weekly table shows a week without a WeekTheme
  And the admin is logged in
  When the admin clicks that week's `Week` cell, enters a title and submits
  Then the week shows the theme next to its week number and the Lessons column is untouched

