    CourseRealizations (one per placeholder Course) for the single hardcoded Semester, including the display-label
    composition, standing in for @CourseRealizationRepository until persistence exists
  [x] Replace the hardcoded ./services.py with a class-based @CourseRealizationRepository-backed
    `RealizationService` (./ports.py and ./repository_sqlite.py), per ../architecture.sdd's Example; it is the
    side of the mutual Semester/Realization pair constructed first, without a `semester_service`, which main.py
    sets as a plain attribute once ../semester/semester.sdd's `SemesterService` exists
  [x] Implement the weekly grid in ./view.py, the realization dropdown scoped to the active Semester, and
    ./routes.py registering `/realizations` with the shareable `realization_id` query parameter
  [x] Validate the Course and Semester ids and a non-empty group label in @RealizationService.add_realization, and
    pass ../semester/semester.sdd's `SemesterService` to ./routes.py's register_routes instead of reaching through the
    two-phase-wired attribute
  [x] Replace a NoTeachWeek's week with a single `No teaching week` entry in @RealizationService's weekly view-model
    through ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd, and render it in ./view.py
  [x] Decide the admin UI for creating a Course and a CourseRealization once ../semester/semester.sdd's Semester
